{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\njh=(\\\"Nine receipts of eight fixed experiments over one defect chain, sharing the structural fixture (snapshot configuration {A,B,C}, a committed configuration entry with {A,B,C,D,E} above it, \\\"\n \\\"a persisted commit index covering it) and the feature-on restart reporting {A,B,C} against the control reporting {A,B,C,D,E}. They successively construct the restart state, observe the split, add \\\"\n \\\"healing, applied-state sampling, the per-node repair phase, the feature-off control, a long run, a configuration change and the leader-side restore. The three receipts cited here are the newest \\\"\n \\\"members of that chain (long run 861a2b3c62bb44d7aed2eee9b95aa15f, configuration change 182740a6d29f4af9a99cf83c49f2e857, leader-side restore 6ff0ef691a0141449142bfa06719bb47); each comparison outcome \\\"\n \\\"is read from its own receipt and no value is combined across them.\\\")\nfor i in d['interpretations']:\n    if i['investigation_id']=='3eae8e12b0574799b781f10f7899dbad-question-0':\n        i['joint_history']=jh\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
